     ddhhccpplleeaasseedd..ccoonnff — DHCP client configuration file

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The dhcpleased(8) daemon is a dynamic host configuration protocol client
     daemon.

     The ddhhccpplleeaasseedd..ccoonnff config file is divided into the following main sec‐
     tions:

     _M_a_c_r_o_s
           Definitions of variables that can be used later, simplifying the
           configuration file.

     _I_n_t_e_r_f_a_c_e_s
           If an interface requires non-default options, they can be defined
           in this section.  Most configurations do not require this.

   MMaaccrrooss
     A macro is defined with a command of the form _n_a_m_e=_v_a_l_u_e.  The macro _n_a_m_e
     can contain letters, digits, and underscores and cannot be a reserved
     word (for example, iinntteerrffaaccee).  Within unquoted arguments, the string
     $_n_a_m_e is later expanded to _v_a_l_u_e.

   IInntteerrffaacceess
     A list of interfaces to overwrite defaults:

     iinntteerrffaaccee _n_a_m_e {_o_p_t_i_o_n _._._.}

             iinntteerrffaaccee options are as follows:

             iiggnnoorree ddnnss
                     Ignore nameservers from leases on this interface.  The
                     default is to not ignore nameservers.

             iiggnnoorree rroouutteess
                     Ignore routes from leases on this interface.  The default
                     is to not ignore routes.

             iiggnnoorree _s_e_r_v_e_r_-_i_p
                     Ignore leases from _s_e_r_v_e_r_-_i_p.  This option can be listed
                     multiple times.  The default is to not ignore servers.

             pprreeffeerr iippvv66
                     Send the IPv6-Only preferred option to the server.  If
                     the server responds with the option, no lease is config‐
                     ured.

             sseenndd cclliieenntt iidd _c_l_i_e_n_t_-_i_d
                     Send the DHCP client identifier option with a value of
                     _c_l_i_e_n_t_-_i_d.  If _c_l_i_e_n_t_-_i_d consists of a series of octets
                     of two-digit hexadecimal numbers separated by colons, the
                     first octet is used as the type and the rest as value.
                     The MAC address 00:53:FF:AA:BB:CC would be configured as:

                           send client id "01:00:53:FF:AA:BB:CC"

                     Otherwise the string _c_l_i_e_n_t_-_i_d is sent verbatim.  The de‐
                     fault is to send the interface's MAC address as client
                     identifier.

                     When _c_l_i_e_n_t_-_i_d is not a hardware address, it is supposed
                     to be sent as hardware type 0 but the majority of DHCP
                     clients and servers do not implement this and neither
                     does ddhhccpplleeaasseedd..ccoonnff.  If a server is encountered that
                     requires this, a 0 byte can be encoded as \0.  The client
                     identifier “foobar” with hardware type 0 would be config‐
                     ured as:

                           send client id "\0foobar"

             sseenndd hhoosstt nnaammee _h_o_s_t_-_n_a_m_e
                     Send the DHCP client host name option with a value of
                     _h_o_s_t_-_n_a_m_e.  The default is to send the name of the host.

             sseenndd nnoo hhoosstt nnaammee
                     Do not send a DHCP host name option.  The default is to
                     send a DHCP host name option with the name of the host.

             sseenndd vveennddoorr ccllaassss iidd _v_e_n_d_o_r_-_c_l_a_s_s_-_i_d
                     Send the DHCP vendor class identifier option with a value
                     of _v_e_n_d_o_r_-_c_l_a_s_s_-_i_d.  The default is to not send a vendor
                     class identifier.

